  , Tuple "heating" "{\"glassbox\":2,\"id\":\"heating\",\"title\":\"Heating controller\",\"notes\":[\"This is the CENTRAL HEATING circuit only, and that restriction is the\",\"finding. A real boiler serves two circuits \\u2014 heating and hot water \\u2014 which\",\"run independently: the water can be reheating while the radiators are\",\"satisfied, and either can be boosted without the other. They are not two\",\"modes of one machine, they are two machines sharing a boiler.\",\"\",\"The format cannot say that. Its options are both bad. Model the product \\u2014\",\"off, ch-only, hw-only, both \\u2014 and six honest states become twenty-four,\",\"then multiply again if a third zone is ever added. Or write two artifacts,\",\"which is correct, and then discover the format has no way to state that two\",\"machines run together, share facts, and contend for one boiler.\",\"\",\"This is the AND-state, and it was predicted: the earlier design notes call\",\"concurrent machines alongside a mode machine exactly that, and answer it\",\"with 'one machine, several instances sharing an environment'. That answer\",\"is still right and is still not implemented \\u2014 `worldFrom` makes one world\",\"for one machine, and nothing composes two.\",\"\",\"So the honest artifact is one circuit, and the missing feature has a name.\",\"\",\"Commands here are the cleanest case in the corpus, because the boiler is a\",\"genuinely two-valued thing: four of the six states want it off and two want\",\"it on, and each says so on entry. It also has the corpus's most defensible\",\"exit command \\u2014 leaving Fault clears the lockout, and there is exactly one\",\"way out of Fault, so no neighbouring state can disagree about it.\"],\"initial\":\"off\",\"clock\":\"minutes\",\"states\":[{\"id\":\"off\",\"label\":\"Off\",\"entry\":[\"burner-off\",\"pump-off\"]},{\"id\":\"frost\",\"label\":\"Frost watch\",\"entry\":[\"burner-off\",\"pump-off\"]},{\"id\":\"satisfied\",\"label\":\"Up to temperature\",